---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { contact } from '../data/site';

const reportHref = `mailto:${contact.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Website accessibility problem')}`;
const reviewed = 'October 31, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility statement | Port of Centralia"
  description="The Port of Centralia's commitment to an accessible website, the standard it follows, known limitations, and how to report a barrier."
>
  <div class="page-head on-dark">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li><span aria-current="page">Accessibility</span></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1>Accessibility statement</h1>
      <p>Everyone should be able to find meetings, documents, and Port services online, whatever device or assistive technology they use.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Our standard</h2>
      <p>
        This website is built to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, the standard
        required of state and local governments under Title II of the Americans with Disabilities Act.
      </p>

      <h2>How we test</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Automated checks with axe and Lighthouse on every page, every time the site is updated.</li>
        <li>Keyboard-only testing of menus, links, and forms.</li>
        <li>Screen reader testing with NVDA (Windows) and VoiceOver (Mac and iPhone).</li>
        <li>Layout checks at 320 pixels wide and at 200% zoom.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <p>We are working on these and will update this page as they are fixed:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Older meeting agendas and minutes were posted as scanned PDFs, which screen readers cannot read. We are
          publishing accessible HTML or tagged PDF versions, newest first. Any older document is available in an
          accessible format on request.
        </li>
        <li>Meeting video captions are being reviewed for accuracy.</li>
        <li>Some links go to pages and documents on sites the Port does not control, such as YouTube and Webex.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="report">Report a problem or request a format</h2>
      <p>
        If something on this site is hard to use, or you need a document in another format, contact us. Tell us the
        page or document and what you need. We will help you get the information.
      </p>
      <ul class="contact-points">
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={reportHref}>{contact.email}</a></li>
        <li><strong>Phone:</strong> <a href={contact.phoneHref}>{contact.phone}</a> ({contact.hours})</li>
        <li><strong>In person or by mail:</strong> {contact.street}, {contact.city}, {contact.region} {contact.postalCode}</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="sources">This statement was last reviewed on {reviewed}.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
